From 7adaa856d2baee58d5a6c1b8e0a403798372bafd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:35:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: sensitive access under app names and the Apps app
 count
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port of the GrapheneOS-era UI5A Settings work, kept inside Android's
Settings structure (KEYBOARD_FIRST_SETTINGS_UX: Apps keeps its place
and its dashboard):

* Settings > Apps > All apps: each row shows the app's effective
  sensitive access under its name instead of its size, e.g.
  "permissions · Location · Contacts · Nearby · +1", with a spoken
  form that names every group. The words, groups, order and rules are
  Sable Start's (DESIGN-KF-D): only grants effective in the app's own
  user count, unreadable state reads "see app info", never "none".
  AppStateSablePrivacyBridge reads it on the ApplicationsState
  background thread; binding a row does no binder call. Returning from
  App info refreshes that app (existing forceUpdate path).
* Top-level Apps summary: "N apps · permissions, network access and
  defaults", counted off the main thread for the current user with the
  upstream InstalledAppCounter rule.

Every specialised app list keeps its upstream summary.
